Information is from an exercise notification to the federal NRC.  is an exercise Caller reported that a 400 barrel (bbl) above ground storage tank breached at a well head facility.  100 bbls of crude oil released into Starvation Reservoir.  Release resulted in 2 injuries and 2 fatalities.  A contractor is on-site containing the spill.

/// THIS IS A DRILL ///

NRC Report; 
CALLER IS REPORTING THAT A POLY FLEX SALT WATER DISPOSAL LINE AT A WELL HEAD FAILED RESULTING IN A SPILL. IT IS UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME IF THERE WAS ANY OIL PRODUCT INVOLVED IN THE SPILL. DUE TO RAIN THE MATERIAL COULD HAVE ENTERED RABBIT GULCH WHICH LEADS TO STARVATION RESERVOIR.

DEQ Callin;
Spill of produced water with potential of having oil although an oil sheen has not been seen, at this point. Due to rains the spill discharged towards Rabbet Gulch which then leads to Starvation Reservoir. The spill is no longer occurring. No surface water was impacted.
